1. e4 { https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pEQdCWwH-YU&list=PLQKBpQZcRycrdFv_RC9rovYN1Wh6F_JPR&index=1 } 1... d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. Bc4 (5. Be2) (5. Bd3) 5... O-O 6. O-O Bg4 { [%csl Gd4,Ge5,Gf3][%cal Ge7e5] } (6... c6 { C6 is done when the bishop move is not possible. } { [%cal Gb8d7] } 7. Re1 Nbd7 { Make sure to claim the center yourself at some point by playing e5. You move your queen for protection of the center. You move your rook to e8 for the same reason (as well as attacking once e5xd4. You move your knight to f8 opening up the bishop again with the goal of getting it on f4. Get an attack going with the minor pieces on the king. } { [%cal Ge7e5,Gd8c7,Gf8e8,Gd7f8] }) (6... Nc6) 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Qxf3 Nc6 { [%csl Gd4] } 9. Be3 (9. d5 { [%csl Ge5,Gd4] } 9... Ne5 { [%cal Ge5c4,Ge5f3] } (9... Nd4 { [%cal Gd4f3,Gd4c2] } 10. Qd3 Nd7 (10... c5 11. dxc6 Nxc6) 11. Be3 Ne5 { [%cal Ge5d3,Ge5c4] } 12. Qxd4 Nf3+ 13. gxf3 Bxd4 14. Bxd4 { [%cal Gf7f5] })) 9... e5 10. dxe5 (10. d5 Ne7 11. Rfe1 Nd7 { Risking your king's safety is possible if the center is locked. You are aiming for a king's side attack here. Keep breaking on the most forward pawn. Can follow up with g5 et cetera. Get to the other side first before they get to our queen's side. Bring back the knights and lift the rook. } { [%csl Gg1][%cal Gf7f5,Gf5f4] }) (10. Rad1 exd4 11. Bxd4 Nxd4 12. Rxd4 Nd7 13. Rdd1 Ne5) 10... Nxe5 11. Qe2 Nxc4 12. Qxc4 Re8 { [%cal Ge8e4] } 13. Rfe1 Nxe4 14. Nxe4 d5 15. Qb3 Rxe4 16. Qxb7 Rb8 17. Qxa7 Rxb2 { [%cal Gb2c2] } 18. Rac1 d4 19. Bd2 Rxe1+ 20. Bxe1 Qg5 { [%cal Gg5c1,Gg5g2,Gb2c2,Gb2g2] } 21. Rd1 Rxc2 22. a4 Be5 { [%csl Gc2,Ge5,Gg5,Gg1] } 23. Bb4 { [%csl Gf8] } 23... c5 24. Bxc5 Rxc5 25. Qxc5 Bh2+ *


