1. e4 { Based on example game in https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eOvOuERnWLw. } 1... d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. Be3 { This is an indication that they play aggresive. } 4... c6 5. Qd2 b5 { [%cal Gd8a5] } 6. Bd3 Nbd7 7. Nf3 Qc7 { Getting ready for an attack for the queen's side. This is an alternative to a5 played by a Super GM. We can deviate. } (7... Qa5) 8. O-O Bg7 9. Bh6 O-O 10. Bxg7 Kxg7 { We have castled because our attack isn't as promising with the king on the other side. Neither is their attack because they have castled too. We play from here in a quiet position. } 11. a4 b4 12. Ne2 c5 13. dxc5 { [%cal Gc7c5] } *


