1. e4 { Opening trap in the Austrian attack variation. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NV3ypecxzYw&list=PLQKBpQZcRycrdFv_RC9rovYN1Wh6F_JPR&index=7 } 1... d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 (4. Bf4 { https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_hZWuxha1Yw&list=PLQKBpQZcRycrdFv_RC9rovYN1Wh6F_JPR&index=43 } 4... Bg7 5. Qd2 c6 6. Bh6 Bxh6 7. Qxh6 Qa5 8. Bd3 c5 9. Ne2 cxd4 10. Nxd4 Qc5 11. Nb3 Qxf2+ 12. Kxf2 Ng4+ { Black is on -2 here. A nice trap in a kind of variation of the 150 attack. } { [%cal Gg4f2,Gg4h6] }) 4... Bg7 5. Nf3 c5 6. dxc5 Qa5 7. Bd2 Qxc5 8. Bd3 O-O 9. Qe2 Nc6 10. Be3 Qb4 11. O-O-O?? { The following idea also works after Rb1. } 11... Nxe4 { [%csl Ge4] } 12. Bxe4 (12. Nxe4 Bxb2+ 13. Kb1 Bc3+ 14. Kc1 Qb2#) 12... Bxc3 13. bxc3 Qxe4 { Taking the bishop and ending the trap. Opponents will want to draw, don't help them. Example from part of a game from here onwards. } 14. Qd3 Qa4 15. g4 Qa3+ 16. Kd2 Qxa2 (16... Na5) 17. h3 *


